      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\int -\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta =$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta )=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta +C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =-\\sqrt{5}\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta +C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
