      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\int (\\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta =$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta )=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta +C, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta )=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta +C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta  & =\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta +\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cosh}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sinh}⁡\\theta +C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
