      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\int 2\\pi {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)={sech}^{2}⁡x\\,⇒\\,\\int {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2\\pi {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\pi \\int {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi \\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
