      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "$\\int (3{csch}^{2}⁡t+10)\\,\\text{d}t=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡t)=-{csch}^{2}⁡t\\,⇒\\,\\int {csch}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=-\\operatorname{coth}⁡t+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{csch}^{2}⁡t+10)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 3{csch}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+\\int 10\\,\\text{d}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3\\int {csch}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+10\\int \\text{d}t \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{coth}⁡t+10t+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
