      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,⇒\\,\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
