      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "$$\n\n$\\int 4{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,⇒\\,\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
